  "has_quantitative_results": true,
  "summary": "The paper proposes a hybrid pipeline where quantum neural network (QNN) feature extractors are used before classical K-Means clustering on Ethereum MCO2 token transaction data. A trained QNN achieves clustering metrics such as Silhouette ≈0.9995 and Davies–Bouldin ≈0.0001 across K=2–6 clusters, outperforming random quantum feature generation runs (best Silhouette ≈0.999994). However, the study reports no qubit counts, circuit architecture, hardware execution, or computational speed comparisons.",
